{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e5d7755eaa27b7b1","name":"Jammer","source":{"id":"source:reference-e5d7755eaa27b7b1","title":"Jammer","revision":18729,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:38:11Z","sha256":"f965e3d27ba66b4b7172f34cc1349f99180b2fe34995e9969053ba1b9b99e8ec","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18729","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Jammer&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e5d7755eaa27b7b1","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["JAMMER\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["EP\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE RESTRICTION\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Suite\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["5,000 (Base)\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Array\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal or Larger\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20,000 (Base)\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Jammers come in many forms, from small Jamming Suites used in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"}," to massive Jamming Arrays carried by some ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},". Not all Jammers are effective enough to alter game statistics- the Jamming Suite in an ",{"tag":"a","children":["ARC-170 Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/ARC-170_Starfighter","referenceId":"reference:fd7701de3a3d42d7"},", for example, has too small an effect on other ships to modify game statistics in any way.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A sensor jamming system is capable of blinding enemy sensors and fire-control computers, making the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," carrying the Jammer a more elusive target. The effectiveness of a Jamming Suite is limited to small craft and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"},", and a single target within 6 squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},") must be selected as the target of the Jammer (a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},"). A Jamming Array affects all enemy ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," within 6 squares of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," carrying it, regardless of the size of those ships.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A ship affected by a Jammer takes penalties on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," checks made to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Communications"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Communications","referenceId":"reference:fa12b21dc3aa7266"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Sensors"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Sensors","referenceId":"reference:1bf2e88f5409e504"},". For a Jamming Suite, the penalty is -4 for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," and -2 for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"},". For a Jamming Array, the penalty is -6 for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},", -4 for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"},", and -2 for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},". This penalty also applies to enemy fire control systems, although it cannot reduce a ship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," ability modifier on attack rolls below +0.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A ",{"tag":"a","children":["System Operator"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/System_Operator","referenceId":"reference:75f56e8f22b64ca4"}," can attempt to overcome the effect of a Jammer. Doing this is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"}," and involves a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check (with the Jammer penalty) opposed by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check of the ship with the Jammer. On a successful result, the Jammed ship takes no penalties from Jamming until the start of the System Operator's next turn.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
